Dear Hiring Professionals,

In searching for a place to go following the completion of my undergraduate studies, I came across your announcement of an opening for a computer engineer. The description of both the position and the company felt like a strong match with me and my work. The values and environment at your company are exactly what I'm looking for in a place of employment, and I'm confident that they will help me thrive as a member of your team.

I've been fostering my skills as a software developer for the last several years, and I think my experience has prepared me well for the work you do at Key Tech. My experience in systems programming with Rust and C has given me a mastery of low-level computing and programming principles, and my work as project lead for both a team and myself has given me the perspective to think about design on both small and large scales. Perhaps most importantly, my hyperfocus on novel and challenging problems has helped me develop a strong mindset for critical thinking that will allow me to keep up pace on the various projects you work on.

I also think that my personality and passion are a good fit for the other people at Key Tech. In my time as an engineer, I find my best work heavily coincides with the work I had the most fun doing. This doesn't mean easy work—in fact, often the opposite—but rather tasks and problems I consider important and/or interesting. I also find that open communication and cheerful collaboration have a major positive impact on the output of a team. Speaking from my past experience as a leader and guider of minds, I believe that, regardless of whether I am a mentor or mentee, I will be able to integrate myself seemlessly into the ecosystem of engineers at your offices.

I look forward to hearing back from you and learning more about your company and the opportunity to join your team. All of your descriptions make it clear that Key Tech is a wonderful place to work, and I would consider it an honor to be there.
